From ac16cd9be5c1a9f7753deaa67ff808f13b1eb8ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JakeStone <208141191+JakeStone594@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:59:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: f_hid: don't call cdev_init while cdev in use
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Backport of upstream 81ebd43cc0d6d "usb: gadget: f_hid: don't call
cdev_init while cdev in use" (Michael Zimmermann, 2026-03-27), plus its
follow-up "usb: gadget: f_hid: Add missing error code" (Ethan Tidmore,
2026-04-02) which supplies the -ENOMEM. CVE-2026-31606, CVSS 3.1 5.5
AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H.

struct cdev is embedded in struct f_hidg, and hidg_bind() called
cdev_init() on it every bind. cdev_init() is memset(cdev, 0, sizeof *cdev)
followed by kobject_init() (fs/char_dev.c:657-663), so a rebind wipes a
kobject that an open fd is still holding a reference to and resets its
refcount to 1.

That an open fd holds such a reference is exactly the property commit
7b96ece4a relies on: chrdev_open() -> cdev_get() ->
kobject_get_unless_zero(&p->kobj) (fs/char_dev.c:364), and
cdev_device_del() -> cdev_del() only kobject_put()s (:600-604) without
freeing or invalidating open fds. So the two interact: the object v6
keeps alive across the unbind is the object whose reference state the
rebind destroys.

Put the cdev on the heap with cdev_alloc() so each bind gets a fresh one.
cdev_alloc() (fs/char_dev.c:639-647) uses ktype_cdev_dynamic, whose
release (:616-624) does cdev_purge(), kfree(p) and kobject_put(parent) —
so the old cdev frees itself at last close and correctly drops its
reference on hidg->dev.

f_hidg_open() can no longer container_of() the embedded member, so it
recovers hidg through the cdev's parent kobject, which cdev_device_add()
sets via cdev_set_parent(cdev, &dev->kobj) (:548). Upstream's form.

Deviations from upstream, both forced by this tree: the error label is
fail_free_descs rather than fail_free_all, and hidg_unbind() has no
destroy_workqueue() — neither exists at 4.14.190.

NOT diverging from a known upstream behaviour: if cdev_device_add() fails
inside cdev_add(), the heap cdev is not freed. That leak is present in
mainline too and only reachable on an allocation/registration failure
path; matching upstream is safer for a backport than inventing a fix.

⚠ This device cannot verify the fix at runtime. CONFIG_DEBUG_LIST is its
only relevant detector and it does not cover this path; SLUB_DEBUG and
DEBUG_OBJECTS are both unset. The damage this prevents — a silently
replaced refcount and kobj.parent — produces no WARN, no poison and no
list check. A clean on-device run therefore evidences CVE-2026-31721
being fixed and says nothing whatever about this one. Correctness here
rests on source review against upstream, not on a device checkpoint.

Verified: compiles rc=0 with zero warnings (positive control on the log:
the CC line for this TU is present in the same capture); .text differs
from the patch-1 object; no &hidg->cdev address-of survives; cdev_init
has 0 call sites where cdev_device_add still has 1, so the zero is
absence rather than a broken probe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013ydNrFirMZjskYMZST87ez
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c
index f544d1d8d..e0a87225e 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ struct f_hidg {
 	struct usb_request		*req;
 
 	struct device			dev;
-	struct cdev			cdev;
+	struct cdev			*cdev;
 	struct usb_function		func;
 
 	struct usb_ep			*in_ep;
@@ -453,8 +453,9 @@ static int f_hidg_release(struct inode *inode, struct file *fd)
 
 static int f_hidg_open(struct inode *inode, struct file *fd)
 {
+	struct kobject *parent = inode->i_cdev->kobj.parent;
 	struct f_hidg *hidg =
-		container_of(inode->i_cdev, struct f_hidg, cdev);
+		container_of(parent, struct f_hidg, dev.kobj);
 
 	fd->private_data = hidg;
 
@@ -829,8 +830,14 @@ static int hidg_bind(struct usb_configuration *c, struct usb_function *f)
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&hidg->write_spinlock, flags);
 
 	/* create char device */
-	cdev_init(&hidg->cdev, &f_hidg_fops);
-	status = cdev_device_add(&hidg->cdev, &hidg->dev);
+	hidg->cdev = cdev_alloc();
+	if (!hidg->cdev) {
+		status = -ENOMEM;
+		goto fail_free_descs;
+	}
+	hidg->cdev->ops = &f_hidg_fops;
+
+	status = cdev_device_add(hidg->cdev, &hidg->dev);
 	if (status)
 		goto fail_free_descs;
 
@@ -1073,7 +1080,7 @@ static void hidg_unbind(struct usb_configuration *c, struct usb_function *f)
 {
 	struct f_hidg *hidg = func_to_hidg(f);
 
-	cdev_device_del(&hidg->cdev, &hidg->dev);
+	cdev_device_del(hidg->cdev, &hidg->dev);
 
 	usb_free_all_descriptors(f);
 }
